  "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-2)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n7{x}^{2}-32x+42=A(x-2)^{2}+B(x-2)+C.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(2)^{2}-32(2)+42 & =A(2-2)^{2}+B(2-2)+C \\\\ 6 & =C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=3$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(3)^{2}-32(3)+42 & =A(3-2)^{2}+B(3-2)+6 \\\\ 9 & =A+B+6 \\\\ B & =3-A.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)^{2}-32(0)+42 & =A(0-2)^{2}+B(0-2)+6 \\\\ 42 & =4A-2B+6 \\\\ 36 & =4A-2B \\\\ B & =2A-18.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-A & =2A-18 \\\\ A & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(1)$ to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =3-7 \\\\ B & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}=\\frac{7}{x-2}-\\frac{4}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{6}{(x-2)^{3}}.\n$$",
